# Almadina ERP — Cursor Project Rule

This rule is an enforcement entry point, not a replacement for repository documentation.

## Read before changing code

- Treat `AGENTS.md` as the authoritative coding contract.
- Read the current `AGENTS.md` and all mandatory canonical references it names before implementation.
- Read the specialist canonical document for the subsystem being changed.
- For UI/UX, JavaScript, CSS, Page/Form/List/Report changes, also read `docs/reference/13_FRONTEND_ARCHITECTURE.md` and its referenced lifecycle standard.
- Inspect the current implementation and relevant tests. Never infer current code from an old conversation.

If instructions conflict with `AGENTS.md`, Product Scope, Architecture Freeze, or another canonical contract, stop and report the discrepancy.

## Branch and scope safety

Before editing:
- Check `git status` and the current branch.
- Do not implement directly on `Develop` or `main`.
- Work on one dedicated feature/fix branch from the latest `Develop`.
- Do not merge, force-push, delete branches, or rewrite shared history unless explicitly requested.

Write the Change Contract required by `docs/reference/07_CHANGE_RULES.md` before code:
Goal, user-visible behavior, in/out of scope, invariants, expected layers/files, permission/security impact, financial impact, schema/migration impact, tests, rollback risk, and docs affected.

If the diff needs unexpected layers/files or changes an invariant, stop and reassess instead of expanding scope automatically.

## Non-negotiable architecture

- `domain/`: pure business rules; no Frappe or outer-layer imports.
- `application/`: use cases/ports; framework-free; no services/infrastructure/UI dependencies.
- `infrastructure/`: Frappe, persistence, files, external-system adapters.
- `services/`: thin RPC boundary with explicit authorization and use-case wiring.
- UI/print/report layers: presentation only; never a second source of costing, lifecycle, or authorization rules.
- Do not expand legacy facades/tombstones for new features.
- Do not introduce active Stock/Warehouse/Reservation/Consumption/Stock Entry/Board Remnant behavior outside Product Scope v1.1.

## Security and financial isolation

- Use Capabilities plus document/lifecycle/stage/assignment scope; never fixed business Role names as authorization.
- `System Manager` is not a factory superuser. `Administrator` is the explicit exception.
- Validate parent/document/file scope; knowing an identifier never grants access.
- Fail closed on invalid/missing identifiers.
- Keep internal financial fields behind the required financial capability; never send them and rely on client-side hiding.

## Frontend and lifecycle

- Server/Application/Domain are authoritative.
- Keep one owner for mutable state and clear ownership for async work, events, timers, and observers.
- Prevent stale responses from mutating newer state.
- Do not mask lifecycle/ownership bugs with random permanent refreshes or competing observers.
- Preserve Arabic-first RTL, desktop/mobile behavior, keyboard flows, focus/accessibility, and loading/error/empty/dirty states.
- No React/Vue/new frontend framework without an explicit ADR/product decision.

## Quality

- Prefer regression tests for bug fixes.
- Never weaken tests to accommodate a regression.
- Migrations must be idempotent and safe on repeated `migrate`.
- Run focused tests, then the relevant broader quality gates.
- Never hide required failures with `continue-on-error`, `|| true`, or equivalent bypasses.

At completion, report: Done, changed files, tests/results, security impact, data/migration impact, explicit non-changes, remaining risks/unverified items, and next step.
